  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying outcomes with probability > 1/n (n = number of outcomes), then computing the average of those outcomes. In this case, no outcome in either lottery exceeds the threshold (25% < 33.3% in A, 25% < 50% in B), so no outcome is probable. The average of probable outcomes is 0 for both. Thus, the reason would be indifferent. The individual, however, prefers B based on the higher maximum gain and (incorrectly) higher probability of that gain. This justification is based on a single outcome (the highest) and its probability, not on the average of probable outcomes. The individual does not consider the concept of 'probable outcomes' or the rule of averaging them. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information considered by the individual (highest outcome and its probability) does not match the information required by the reason (set of outcomes exceeding 1/n and their average). The justification rule (favoring higher max gain and higher probability of it) is different from the reason's rule (favoring higher average of probable outcomes). Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
